<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Overview">Overview</span></h2>
<p>Items for the Single player campaign are all stored in the Toolset's <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Resource%20palette" title="Resource palette">Resource palette</a>, under the Item Category. They are as such files describing what an Item is and what it looks like, but they do not tell who or where it is in the game. It is sort of independent resource in that way. Any other Resource however can make use of it as they want.
</p><p>Items, as with any other Resource follow a <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Naming%20conventions#Resource_Naming_Convention" title="Naming conventions">Naming convention</a>, to make it easier to navigate the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Resource%20palette" title="Resource palette">Resource palette</a>.
</p><p>Unlike in Neverwinter Nights, items can't be placed on the floor. They can only be stored in an inventory of some kind.
</p><p>Items are stored in *.UTI File format.
</p>
